Lovelace Testing & Debugging Guide:

1. Development Workflow:
   - Use Hot Module Replacement with Vite
   - Create development server script in package.json
   - Create copy-to-hass.js to deploy to dev environment
   - Use localStorage.setItem('lovelace-dev-tools', true) to enable dev tools
   - Enable logging during development, disable in production
   - Create demo configuration in dev-environment

2. Testing Framework:
   - Unit tests with Vitest or Jest
   - Use testing-library for component testing
   - Mock HomeAssistant interface for isolated tests
   - Test core functionality without actual HA instance
   - Verify state management and rendering logic
   - Test both normal and error states

3. Common Issues & Solutions:
   - Shadow DOM styling issues: use ::part() and constructStylesheet
   - Custom element registration: check for conflicts
   - Event listener leaks: validate disconnectedCallback cleanup
   - Memory leaks: watch for retained references
   - Undefined properties: handle loading states correctly
   - Re-rendering issues: verify property/state changes trigger updates

4. Performance Testing:
   - Use Chrome DevTools Performance tab
   - Monitor memory usage during long sessions
   - Check rendering times with performance.measure()
   - Identify expensive operations for optimization
   - Test with both small and large data sets
   - Profile on lower-powered devices when possible

5. Release Checklist:
   - Version bump in package.json and CHANGELOG
   - Run linting and tests
   - Build in production mode
   - Test in clean Home Assistant instance
   - Verify HACS compatibility
   - Test installation from ZIP archive

Implement structured logging with levels (debug, info, warn, error) to aid troubleshooting.